{
  "_readme": [
    "This is the one file to edit. Change any text, save, then commit (see README).",
    "highlights: 3-4 very short bullets (about five words each). specs: label/value pairs.",
    "robot.front: which way the robot faces at the start. \"auto\" points the intake at the viewer; or use +x, -x, +z, -z.",
    "match: words from Onshape sub-assembly or part names. Parts that match nothing go to Frame & Structure.",
    "hideWhenFocused: parts hidden while that subsystem is selected (e.g. panels that block the view). frameOn: parts the camera centers on when the subsystem is selected (default: all of them). includeMechanisms: moving parts shown solid with this subsystem even though they belong to another (the brain pan cover with Electrical).",
    "mechanisms: moving parts (CAD coordinates in meters). \"fourbar\" = parallel four-bar: crank pivot, follower pivot and the crank's far joint; crank / followerLinks / swivel.parts name whole sub-assemblies or parts (anywhere below the mechanism's assembly) that ride that link, and screws, nuts, rivets and belts follow the part they are fastened to. swivel: parts hinged on the four-bar's moving link that swing clear of the bumper (the kicker ramp). ownsParts: false keeps the moving parts in their own subsystem (the brain pan cover stays Frame, its slider shows under Electrical). After changing, run: npm run model"
  ],
